\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{P}_{\boldsymbol{k}\rightarrow\boldsymbol{k}'} & =\mathcal{P}_{\boldsymbol{k}\rightarrow\boldsymbol{k}'}^{I}+\mathcal{P}_{\boldsymbol{k}\rightarrow\boldsymbol{k}'}^{II}\\
 & =\Lambda_{I}\left(\boldsymbol{k},\boldsymbol{k}'\right)S\left(\boldsymbol{k}-\boldsymbol{k}',\varepsilon_{\boldsymbol{k}}-\varepsilon_{\boldsymbol{k}'}\right)+\sum_{\bm{q}}\Lambda_{II}\left(\boldsymbol{k},\boldsymbol{k}'\right)\frac{\hbar}{2M\omega_{\boldsymbol{k}-\boldsymbol{k}'-\boldsymbol{q}}}\left[1+n_{B}\left(\hbar\omega_{\boldsymbol{k}-\boldsymbol{k}'-\boldsymbol{q}}\right)\right]S\left(\boldsymbol{k}-\boldsymbol{k}',\varepsilon_{\boldsymbol{k}}-\varepsilon_{\boldsymbol{k}'}+\omega_{\boldsymbol{k}-\boldsymbol{k}'-\boldsymbol{q}}\right)
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the high temperature limit where the phonons are in the equipartition
 regime, we have a transition rate given by 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\mathcal{P}_{\boldsymbol{k}\rightarrow\boldsymbol{k}'}=\Lambda_{I}\left(\boldsymbol{k},\boldsymbol{k}'\right)S\left(\boldsymbol{k}-\boldsymbol{k}',\varepsilon_{\boldsymbol{k}}-\varepsilon_{\boldsymbol{k}'}\right)+\frac{k_{b}T}{2}\sum_{\bm{q}}\Lambda_{II}\left(\boldsymbol{k},\boldsymbol{k}'\right)\frac{S\left(\boldsymbol{k}-\boldsymbol{k}',\varepsilon_{\boldsymbol{k}}-\varepsilon_{\boldsymbol{k}'}+\omega_{\boldsymbol{k}-\boldsymbol{k}'-\boldsymbol{q}}\right)}{M\omega_{\boldsymbol{k}-\boldsymbol{k}'-\boldsymbol{q}\lambda}^{2}}.
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

